		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">49</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words
1. As I process 1000 numbers, it will be difficult for me to remember the counts in my memory. So, I will take a paper and write down count of odd and count of even. That way, for every number, I will update the paper and I don't need to worry about forgetting.
2. If it is a small list like 3 or 5 numbers, then it is easy for me to remember how many numbers I checked. But 1000 is a large number. So, to avoid checking more than 1000, I will also keep a count of how many numbers I checked until now. Whenever it reached 1000, I will stop processing. This count also, I will write on a paper (just like odd count and even count).</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">233.55396825396826</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3032.4979450950955</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">213.6455758623414</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words
1. As I process 1000 numbers, it will be difficult for me to remember the counts in my memory. So, I will take a paper and write down count of odd and count of even. That way, for every number, I will update the paper and I don't need to worry about forgetting.
2. If it is a small list like 3 or 5 numbers, then it is easy for me to remember how many numbers I checked. But 1000 is a large number. So, to avoid checking more than 1000, I will also keep a count of how many numbers I checked until now. Whenever it reached 1000, I will stop processing. This count also, I will write on a paper (just like odd count and even count).</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">202.21875</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">50</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Read list size
2. Write down 3 counts - numberCount, oddCount and evenCount. Initially all 3 of them will be 0.
3. Take a number
4. Check if it is odd
5. If yes, increase oddCount
6. Otherwise increase evenCount
7. In any case, increase numberCount
8. Repeat steps 3 to 7 until numberCount becomes same as listSize
9. By the end, oddCount and evenCount will have the count of odd numbers and even numbers</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">233.55396825396826</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3304.844692832437</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">213.6455758623414</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Read list size
2. Write down 3 counts - numberCount, oddCount and evenCount. Initially all 3 of them will be 0.
3. Take a number
4. Check if it is odd
5. If yes, increase oddCount
6. Otherwise increase evenCount
7. In any case, increase numberCount
8. Repeat steps 3 to 7 until numberCount becomes same as listSize
9. By the end, oddCount and evenCount will have the count of odd numbers and even numbers</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">202.21875</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
